This is Schanuel's Conjecture — one of the most famous open problems in transcendental number theory, unsolved since it was posed by Schanuel in the 1960s. Even special cases (such as the algebraic independence of $e$ and $\pi$, which would follow from the $n=2$ instance with $z_1=1, z_2=\pi i$) remain open. No proof is known, and the conjecture is far beyond current techniques.

